      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfyui-custom-scripts",
        "ver": "f2838ed5e59de4d73cde5c98354b87a8d3200190",
        "Node name for S&R": "ShowText|pysssss",
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {},
          "version": "7.5.1"
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "A 20-something woman with a soft, round face and long, dark hair that falls in soft waves over her shoulders. She is standing in a sunlit room, her body angled slightly to the side as she looks at the camera with a quiet expression. She wears a white t-shirt with red text and light-wash blue jeans, which are slightly unbuttoned to reveal her midriff. Her hands are behind her head, gently holding her hair back. The scene is warm and natural; sunlight filters through a window behind her, creating strong contrast on the wall and casting defined cool shadows under her arms. A clean line of skin glows softly from the warmth of the day.\n\nIn this Nai3 anime style image: di Lilei (Dilraba) has an elegant yet casual look — she's styled in high fashion as if for an editorial shoot— but it's not about being bold or loud; it’s more about presence. In this case, we see Di Lilei from one end of an intimate space: possibly by a window or near some sort of table set up for reading or work? It could be any place where time seems to move slow.\n\nThe lighting is natural daylight at around 6500K color temperature – crisp but still dreamy – perfecting all those details on skin texture and fabric patterns that will make you want to take off your clothes just because you know they're so good.\n\nThis makes us think: what do we get when we combine these two things? We have something like *a* real person who might be too reserved for public life but also very much into self-expression through artful dressings...and then there's DILRABA herself! This version isn't just another model; it feels like part of our own story now – even if only once per year.\n\nIt’s all about how people find their way into each other’s world while looking outwards into different lives — both inner ones and outer ones — without having to say anything first.\n\nAnd so here she stands again against nature’s simple beauty…not trying too hard...just being...right there...\n\nShe doesn’t need anything else than that little bit more light across everything else before going back home after work every day?\n\nLet me tell you what I really care about most right now:\n\nThat small thing between us.\nThe way we catch each other's eyes,\nthe momentary pause,\nand then—\nour hearts start moving again.\nWe don't have enough words,\nbut enough feelings.\nBecause love does not require language;\nit already exists within us.\nAnd today?\nI am ready for it.\nWith my hand held up high...\nas if nothing else matters except this one breathless second where I finally let go…of my past…\n\nAnd somewhere down below...\n\nThere was no need even though I had been wearing them since morning…\nbecause they were never meant to last long enough anyway!\n\nBut here—and now—\n\nYes—that would be true:\nif only someone said yes before letting go!\nOr maybe even better:\nif someone showed up just when I needed them most…in exactly this same kind of moment...\n\nSo let’s keep going along these lines until next time!\nWhen something new comes around—not always expected—but always welcome!\n\nFor now?\n\nYou can call me “Lilei”  \nor “Di Lilei”  \nor simply \"the girl\" who knows how many times he must say 'no' before saying 'yes’ again\n\nNo matter which name gets used later on,\n\nthis single photograph remains etched deep inside my mind…\n\nAs well as yours…\n\nFrom memory—a silent echo—coming from far away,\n\nstill waiting…\n\nto return home once more...\n\nTo open up our door together again…with full heart & soul..."
      ]
    },
